          "source_quote": "τοῦ νῦν μόνου μακροθύμου καὶ ἀγαθοῦ",
          "english_quote": "who alone is now patient and good",
          "issue": "The main rendering is grammatically defensible and preserves the supplied μόνου. However, the lexical note treats its agreement with God as conclusively determining the focus of exclusivity. Agreement supports the person-exclusive reading, but the contrast between present patience and the ensuing judgment also raises a possible present-mode interpretation, ‘who is now only patient and good.’ That less straightforward interpretation is neither evaluated nor preserved as uncertainty. It must also be distinguished from ‘only for now,’ which can suggest that the attributes themselves will cease.",
          "suggested_revision": "Retain the supplied μόνου and qualify the lexical rationale. Add a meaning-level source_issues note identifying ‘who alone is now patient and good’ as the straightforward person-exclusive reading and explaining the contextual pressure toward a present-mode reading without certifying that alternative. Seek comparable usage in this author or period before excluding it categorically. Do not silently substitute μόνον or change the main text merely to harmonize the theology. Any revised wording or note requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
